    "q-130548": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130548",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-7,3],$ compute $P(-5<X\\le 1).$",
      "worked_solution": "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-7,3],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10},\\, & -7\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-5<X\\le 1) & ={\\int }_{-5}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-5}^{1}\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-5)}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-130548-a",
