      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{7}{3}],$ compute $P(X>1).$",
      "worked_solution": "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{7}{3}],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2},\\, & \\frac{1}{3}\\le x\\le \\frac{7}{3}, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1) & =P(1<X\\le \\frac{7}{3}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{7/3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{7/3}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{3}-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
