    "q-130689": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130689",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Given that the continuous random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,11],$ compute $P(W\\ge 7).$",
      "worked_solution": "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $W$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le w\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,11],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8},\\, & 3\\le w\\le 11, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W\\ge 7) & =P(7\\le W\\le 11) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{7}^{11}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{7}^{11}\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{11-7}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
