    "q-89982": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89982",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Given that the continuous random variable $Y$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-3,7],$ compute $P(Y>3).$",
      "worked_solution": "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $Y$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le y\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $Y$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-3,7],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10},\\, & -3\\le y\\le 7, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y>3) & =P(3<Y<7) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{7}f(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{7}\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{7-3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-89982-a",
